1. For each study, calculate the risk ratio (RR) using the formula: RR = (events_gdft/n_gdft) / (events_control/n_control)
2. Calculate the standard error (SE) of the log-RR using the formula: SE = sqrt(1/n_gdft + 1/n_control)
3. Calculate the log-RR using the formula: log-RR = log(RR)
4. Calculate the 95% confidence interval of the log-RR using the formula: CI95 = [log-RR - 1.96 \* SE, log-RR + 1.96 \* SE]
5. Back-transform the CI95 to get the 95% confidence interval of the RR using the formula: CI95 = [exp(CI95[0]), exp(CI95[1])]

